          },
          "code": "FORM_FOR_CREATE_APPOINTMENTS",
          "id": "1770741197495",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770741197497_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Objective**  \nUsing **only** the Opportunity Details payload below (and the provided system time variables):  \n`{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Context}}`  \ncreate a **recordWidget** with `id=\"SDA-CreateAppointment-opportunities\"` to schedule a **customer-facing** appointment derived from the recommendation intent and the opportunity context. The output must be written so it is appropriate to send to the customer as a meeting invite (clear purpose, shared outcomes, and a concrete agenda).\n\n---\n## Strict Data Usage Policy (must follow)\n- **Use only the information explicitly present** in `{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Context}}` plus:\n  - `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`\n  - `{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}`\n- **Do not use external knowledge, assumptions, prior conversations, or inferred facts.**\n- **Do not fabricate** names, stakeholders, timelines, risks, products, amounts, stages, close dates, effective dates, decision processes, or next steps that are not present in the payload.\n- If required details are missing, use **neutral placeholders** such as “customer stakeholders,” “customer business owner,” “customer technical team,” “procurement/legal stakeholders,” or “sales/account team.”\n- If the recommendation intent is missing or unclear, use a safe generic customer-facing meeting type aligned to execution, e.g., **“Working Session — Opportunity Alignment (<Product/Solution> / <Account>)”** using placeholders as needed.\n\n---\n## Authoring Rules\n### 1) Subject (meeting title)\n- Convert the recommendation intent into a **customer-friendly**, **collaborative**, imperative subject (do not copy the recommendation title verbatim).\n- Use a strong action verb that works for both parties (e.g., **Align, Review, Confirm, Plan, Finalize, Validate**).\n- Include **solution/product** and **account/opportunity name** *only if available in the payload*.\n- Keep it **one crisp professional line**.\n**Examples (generic, non-fabricated):**\n- `Align on Next Steps — Supplier Relationship Hub (Acme Corp)`\n- `Review Scope and Timeline — Supplier Relationship Hub (customer stakeholders)`\n\n### 2) Description (customer-oriented)\n- Output **HTML** (no heading tags such as `<h1>–<h6>`).\n- Write **5 ~ 10 concise sentences** in a tone suitable for a customer invite (clear, collaborative, outcome-focused; avoid internal sales phrasing like “close the deal”).\n- The description must:\n  - State a **shared meeting purpose** tied to the recommendation intent (focus on customer objectives and decisions needed)\n  - Include a **detailed agenda with exactly 3–4 numbered points** (e.g., scope, stakeholders/decision process, timeline/dependencies, risks/open items, next steps)\n  - Identify **participants** using neutral placeholders if unknown\n  - Define the **desired outcome** (e.g., agreed plan/decision/next steps) and assign a **clear next step and owner** using placeholders if needed\n  - Reference **opportunity details only if present** (e.g., product/solution, stage, amount, close date, risks). If not present, omit.\n\n### 3) Dates, time, duration\n- `startDate`: `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}` (type: `date`)\n- `startTime`: `{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}` **rounded to nearest 30 minutes**, formatted as `HH:MM:SS AM/PM` (type: `text`)\n- `duration`: default to **30** minutes (type: `number`)  \n  - If rounding/date math isn’t supported, still set duration to 30 and note “30‑min duration” in the description.\n\n### 4) Tone\n- Professional and customer-ready.  \n- No internal-only language (e.g., “win probability,” “deal size,” “closing,” “pipeline,” “rep actions”) unless those exact terms appear in the payload (and even then, prefer neutral phrasing).\n\n---\n## Hidden System Field\nInclude a hidden system field:\n- `id`: `\"optyNumber\"`\n- `value`: `opportunity.OptyNumber` (from the input context only)\n- `hidden`: `true`\n\n---\n## Expected Output Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"SDA-CreateAppointment-opportunities\",\n  \"fields\": [\n    { \"id\": \"subject\", \"label\": \"Subject\", \"value\": \"<imperative, customer-friendly subject>\", \"type\": \"text\" },\n { \"id\": \"duration\", \"label\": \"Duration (Minutes)\", \"value\": 30, \"type\": \"number\" },\n    { \"id\": \"startDate\", \"label\": \"Start Date\", \"value\": \"{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\", \"type\": \"date\" },\n    { \"id\": \"startTime\", \"label\": \"Start Time (GMT)\", \"value\": \"<HH:MM:SS AM/PM rounded to 30-min>\", \"type\": \"text\" },\n    { \"id\": \"description\", \"label\": \"Description\", \"value\": \"<HTML, 5–10 sentences, includes a 3–4 point numbered agenda>\", \"type\": \"text\" },\n    { \"id\": \"optyNumber\", \"label\": \"optyNumber\", \"value\": \"<opportunity.OptyNumber>\", \"type\": \"system\", \"hidden\": true }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n## Validation Checklist\n- No content appears that is not grounded in the provided payload/system time variables.\n- Subject is imperative and **customer-friendly** (collaborative wording).\n- Description is **HTML**, **5–10 sentences**, customer-oriented, and includes a **3–4 point numbered agenda**.\n- Avoids internal sales phrasing unless explicitly present in the payload.\n- `optyNumber` is populated from the payload and hidden.\n- `startTime` is `HH:MM:SS AM/PM` rounded to 30 minutes; duration is 30.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
