            "name": "FormCreateNote"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FORMCREATENOTE",
          "id": "1771836731724",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771836731725_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Objective**  \nUsing **only** the Opportunity Details payload below, generate:  \n- A concise, professional note title (one line).  \n- A focused **private internal note in HTML** (3–6 sentences).  \nDo **not** invent, infer, assume, or use any information not explicitly present in the payload.\n\n---\n\n## Input  \n`{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Context}}`\n\n---\n\n## Strict Data Usage Policy (must follow)\n- **Source of truth:** Only use data explicitly present in the input payload (e.g., opportunity name, stage, product/solution, amount, close date, stakeholders, risks, competitors, next steps).  \n- **No external knowledge:** Do not use prior conversation context, general industry knowledge, or assumptions.  \n- **No fabrication:** If a detail is missing, **omit it** (do **not** add placeholders).  \n- **PII:** Treat as internal/private. Do not include customer PII beyond what appears in the input.\n\n---\n\n## Authoring Rules\n\n### Title\n- One line, professional, action-oriented or topic-focused.  \n- Use examples only as a pattern (do not copy unless supported by input):  \n  - `Competitive Posture — <Opportunity Name>`  \n  - `Risk Review — Stage <X> Close <Date>` (only if stage/close date exist in payload)  \n- Avoid acronyms unless they appear in the input.\n\n### Note Body (HTML required)\n- The note **must be valid HTML** and **must not include heading tags** (`<h1>`–`<h6>`).  \n- Keep it concise: **5 ~ 10 sentences total**.\n- Use clean formatting similar to the appointment description:\n  - use line breaks  where needed .\n  - If you need bullets, use **one** `<ul><li>` list and keep bullets short (optional). Bullets do not replace the 5 ~ 10 sentence requirement unless each bullet is a complete sentence.\n- Content guidance:\n  - Summarize only the key facts relevant for internal coordination that are **present in the payload** (stage, solution/product, timing, amount, stakeholders, risks/blockers, competitors, key events, next steps).\n  - Keep statements evidence-based and tied directly to the input (e.g., “The opportunity is at Stage X…”).\n  - Avoid assumptions, speculative language, and new commitments.\n  - If dates/numbers are present, preserve the **original formats** (do not reformat).\n\n---\n\n## Output Schema  \nReturn a `recordWidget`:\n\n- `id`: `\"SDA-CreateNote-opportunities\"`  \n- `fields`:  \n  - `{ id: \"title\", label: \"Title\", value: \"<one-line professional title>\", type: \"text\" }`  \n  - `{ id: \"note\", label: \"Note\", value: \"<VALID HTML, 3–6 sentences, only provided data>\", type: \"text\" }`  \n  - `{ id: \"optyNumber\", label: \"optyNumber\", value: opportunity.OptyNumber, type: \"system\", hidden: true }`\n\n---\n\n## Validation\n- Title is one line, professional, and derived only from provided data.\n- Note is **valid HTML**, contains **3–6 sentences**, includes **no heading tags**, and is strictly based on the input (no placeholders, no invented details).\n- `optyNumber` is populated from the payload and hidden."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_RECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create Task"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_TASK",
          "id": "1771837586894",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771837586895_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Objective**  \nUsing **only** the Opportunity Details payload below, generate a **customer-centric** internal task that helps the team deliver a high-quality customer experience and move the opportunity forward responsibly. Produce:  \n- **Subject:** one-line, action-oriented task subject (customer-outcome oriented).  \n- **Description:** **2–5 sentence task description in valid HTML** that frames the work in terms of customer needs, decisions, and readiness.  \nDo **not** invent, infer, assume, or guess any information not present in the payload.\n\n---\n## Input  \n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Context}}\n\n---\n## Strict Data Usage Policy (must follow)\n- **Source of truth:** Only use fields explicitly present in the input payload (e.g., opportunity name, stage, product/solution, amount, close date, stakeholders, risks, competitors, next steps, activities).  \n- **No external knowledge:** Do not use prior conversation context or general knowledge.  \n- **No fabrication:** If a detail is missing, **omit it** (do **not** add placeholders).  \n- **PII:** Treat as internal/private. Do not include customer PII beyond what appears in the input.\n\n---\n## Authoring Rules\n### Tone\nProfessional, concise, factual; internal audience. Write with a **customer-first lens** (focus on clarity, responsiveness, and removing customer blockers), while keeping content strictly payload-backed.\n\n### Subject\n- One line; start with an action verb aligned to the task (e.g., **Follow Up, Confirm, Prepare, Review, Coordinate, Schedule, Validate, Share**).\n- Make the subject **customer-outcome oriented** (e.g., confirm customer decision items, provide requested info, align on scope/timeline), while staying factual.\n- Include relevant specifics **only if present** (product/solution, opportunity name, stage, timing cues, customer request/next step).\n- Avoid acronyms unless present in input.\n\n### Description (HTML required)\n- The description **must be valid HTML** and **must not include heading tags** (`<h1>`–`<h6>`).\n- Length: **2–5 sentences total**.\n- Formatting:\n  - Prefer `<p>...</p>` paragraphs; use line breaks only when necessary.\n  - Do not use section headers like “Purpose:” or “Next steps:”.\n- Content (customer-centric framing, payload-only facts):\n  - State **what to do** in a way that supports the customer’s evaluation/decision (e.g., share clarifications, confirm requirements, align stakeholders, address identified risks/blockers) **only if those items are present** in the payload.\n  - State **why it matters for the customer** (e.g., enables decision, reduces risk, confirms scope/timeline) without adding new claims, commitments, or dates beyond what’s provided.\n  - If stage/close date/risks/competitors/next steps exist in the payload, you may reference them verbatim to ground urgency and context.\n  - No assumptions, no new commitments, no placeholders, and preserve original date/number formats (do not reformat).\n\n### Due Date\n- Default to the current date: `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}` (type: `date`)\n\n### Type\n- Task type must be selected from the provided options only:  \n  `options: {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_THE_REQUIRED_ATTRIBUTES.$output.result}}`\n\n---\n## Output Schema  \nReturn a `recordWidget`:\n- `id`: `\"SDA-CreateTask-opportunities\"`\n- `fields`:  \n  - `{ id: \"subject\", label: \"Subject\", value: \"<one-line customer-outcome oriented task subject using only provided data>\", type: \"text\" }`  \n  - `{ id: \"description\", label: \"Description\", value: \"<VALID HTML, 2–5 sentences, customer-centric framing, only provided data>\", type: \"text\" }`  \n  - `{ id: \"dueDate\", label: \"Due Date\", value: \"{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\", type: \"date\" }`  \n  - `{ id: \"type\", label: \"Type\", value: \"\", type: \"select\", options: {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_THE_REQUIRED_ATTRIBUTES.$output.result}} }`  \n  - `{ id: \"optyNumber\", label: \"optyNumber\", value: opportunity.OptyNumber, type: \"system\", hidden: true }`\n\n---\n## Validation\n- Subject is one line, action-oriented, and **customer-outcome oriented**, derived only from the provided data.\n- Description is **valid HTML**, contains **2–5 sentences**, includes **no heading tags**, and is strictly based on the input (no invented details, no placeholders).\n- Description avoids internal-only selling language (e.g., “close the deal,” “win probability”) unless explicitly present in the payload.\n- `dueDate` equals `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`.\n- `optyNumber` is populated from the payload and hidden."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
